   "source": [
    "# GitHub → Telegram Random Photo Publisher\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook is designed to run locally in Jupyter **or automatically through GitHub Actions**.\n",
    "\n",
    "Each run:\n",
    "1. Lists image files in this repository's `images/` folder.\n",
    "2. Chooses a random image, avoiding the immediately previous image when possible.\n",
    "3. Chooses a random caption from `comments.txt`.\n",
    "4. Posts the photo to a Telegram channel.\n",
    "5. Deletes the previous bot-posted photo, if one is recorded.\n",
    "6. Saves the latest Telegram message ID in `state.json`.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Before running\n",
    "- Add images to `images/` (JPG, JPEG, PNG, or WEBP; keep each under 10 MB).\n",
    "- Add one caption/comment per line to `comments.txt`.\n",
    "- Add your Telegram bot as a channel administrator with permission to post and delete messages.\n",
    "- Configure `TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` and `TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID` as environment variables / GitHub Actions secrets.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Security:** Never put your bot token in this notebook or commit it to GitHub.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f8496e11",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Dependencies (GitHub Actions installs these automatically)\n",
    "%pip -q install requests\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "d3849551",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import mimetypes\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "from datetime import datetime, timezone\n",
    "\n",
    "import requests\n",
    "\n",
    "# Repository settings.\n",
    "# In GitHub Actions, GITHUB_REPOSITORY is automatically set to \"owner/repo\".\n",
    "REPOSITORY = os.getenv(\"GITHUB_REPOSITORY\", \"YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_REPOSITORY\")\n",
    "BRANCH = os.getenv(\"GITHUB_REF_NAME\", \"main\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Telegram credentials are supplied through environment variables.\n",
    "BOT_TOKEN = os.getenv(\"TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN\", \"\").strip()\n",
    "CHAT_ID = os.getenv(\"TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID\", \"\").strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Files in the repository.\n",
    "IMAGE_DIR = Path(\"images\")\n",
    "COMMENTS_FILE = Path(\"comments.txt\")\n",
    "STATE_FILE = Path(\"state.json\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set True to remove the previous bot-posted photo after a new one is successfully posted.\n",
    "DELETE_PREVIOUS_POST = True\n",
    "\n",
    "# Telegram Bot API upload limit for photos is 10 MB.\n",
    "MAX_IMAGE_BYTES = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n",
    "\n",
    "if not BOT_TOKEN:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"Missing TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN environment variable.\")\n",
    "if not CHAT_ID:\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\"Missing TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID environment variable.\")\n",
    "if \"/\" not in REPOSITORY or REPOSITORY.startswith(\"YOUR_\"):\n",
    "    raise RuntimeError(\n",
    "        \"Set GITHUB_REPOSITORY to 'owner/repo' when running locally, \"\n",
    "        \"or run this notebook through GitHub Actions.\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "OWNER, REPO = REPOSITORY.split(\"/\", 1)\n",
    "API_BASE = f\"https://api.telegram.org/bot{BOT_TOKEN}\"\n",
    "GITHUB_API = f\"https://api.github.com/repos/{OWNER}/{REPO}\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Repository: {REPOSITORY}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Branch: {BRANCH}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Target Telegram chat: {CHAT_ID}\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "ef0770d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def load_state():\n",
    "    if not STATE_FILE.exists():\n",
    "        return {}\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return json.loads(STATE_FILE.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n",
    "    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n",
    "        return {}\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def save_state(state):\n",
    "    STATE_FILE.write_text(\n",
    "        json.dumps(state, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\\\n\",\n",
    "        encoding=\"utf-8\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def telegram_call(method, *, data=None, files=None, timeout=60):

    url = f"{API_BASE}/{method}"

    response = requests.post(
        url,
        data=data,
        files=files,
        timeout=timeout
    )

    try:
        payload = response.json()
    except ValueError:
        raise RuntimeError(
            f"Telegram returned HTTP {response.status_code} "
            "with a non-JSON response."
        )

    if not response.ok or not payload.get("ok"):
        description = payload.get(
            "description",
            "Unknown Telegram API error"
        )

        error_code = payload.get("error_code", response.status_code)

        raise RuntimeError(
            f"Telegram API error: {error_code} - {description}"
        )

    return payload["result"]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def list_repository_images():\n",
    "    url = f\"{GITHUB_API}/contents/images\"\n",
    "    headers = {\"Accept\": \"application/vnd.github+json\"}\n",
    "    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers, timeout=30)\n",
    "    response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "\n",
    "    allowed = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".webp\"}\n",
    "    items = response.json()\n",
    "\n",
    "    return [\n",
    "        item for item in items\n",
    "        if item.get(\"type\") == \"file\"\n",
    "        and Path(item.get(\"name\", \"\")).suffix.lower() in allowed\n",
    "        and item.get(\"download_url\")\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def load_comments():\n",
    "    url = f\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{OWNER}/{REPO}/{BRANCH}/comments.txt\"\n",
    "    response = requests.get(url, timeout=30)\n",
    "    response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "\n",
    "    comments = [\n",
    "        line.strip()\n",
    "        for line in response.text.splitlines()\n",
    "        if line.strip() and not line.lstrip().startswith(\"#\")\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not comments:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\"comments.txt is empty. Add at least one caption.\")\n",
    "    return comments\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "fdc8c3ea",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def publish_random_photo():\n",
    "    state = load_state()\n",
    "    images = list_repository_images()\n",
    "\n",
    "    if not images:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\"No supported images found in the repository's images/ folder.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    previous_name = state.get(\"last_image\")\n",
    "    candidates = [img for img in images if img[\"name\"] != previous_name]\n",
    "    if not candidates:\n",
    "        candidates = images\n",
    "\n",
    "    chosen = random.choice(candidates)\n",
    "    comments = load_comments()\n",
    "    caption = random.choice(comments)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Download from the public GitHub repository, then upload bytes to Telegram.\n",
    "    image_response = requests.get(chosen[\"download_url\"], timeout=60)\n",
    "    image_response.raise_for_status()\n",
    "    image_bytes = image_response.content\n",
    "\n",
    "    if len(image_bytes) > MAX_IMAGE_BYTES:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(\n",
    "            f\"{chosen['name']} is {len(image_bytes):,} bytes; \"\n",
    "            \"Telegram photo uploads must be no larger than 10 MB. \"\n",
    "            \"Resize/compress it and commit the smaller image.\"\n",
    "        )\n",
    "\n",
    "    mime_type = mimetypes.guess_type(chosen[\"name\"])[0] or \"application/octet-stream\"\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Post first. If posting fails, the previous post remains intact.\n",
    "    result = telegram_call(\n",
    "        \"sendPhoto\",\n",
    "        data={\n",
    "            \"chat_id\": CHAT_ID,\n",
    "            \"caption\": caption[:1024],\n",
    "        },\n",
    "        files={\n",
    "            \"photo\": (chosen[\"name\"], image_bytes, mime_type)\n",
    "        },\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    new_message_id = result[\"message_id\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Delete the previous post only after the new one was posted successfully.\n",
    "    old_message_id = state.get(\"last_message_id\")\n",
    "    if DELETE_PREVIOUS_POST and old_message_id:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            telegram_call(\n",
    "                \"deleteMessage\",\n",
    "                data={\n",
    "                    \"chat_id\": CHAT_ID,\n",
    "                    \"message_id\": old_message_id,\n",
    "                },\n",
    "            )\n",
    "            print(f\"Deleted previous Telegram message: {old_message_id}\")\n",
    "        except Exception as exc:\n",
    "            # Continue and record the new post; the previous message may be too old\n",
    "            # or the bot may lack the required channel administrator permission.\n",
    "            print(f\"Could not delete previous message {old_message_id}: {exc}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    state.update({\n",
    "        \"last_image\": chosen[\"name\"],\n",
    "        \"last_message_id\": new_message_id,\n",
    "        \"chat_id\": str(CHAT_ID),\n",
    "        \"last_caption\": caption[:1024],\n",
    "        \"posted_at_utc\": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    save_state(state)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f\"Posted: {chosen['name']}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Caption: {caption}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Telegram message ID: {new_message_id}\")\n",
    "    print(\"state.json updated.\")\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run one publication.\n",
    "publication_result = publish_random_photo()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "c670edc0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Local testing\n",
    "\n",
    "For a local test, set the environment variables before launching Jupyter, for example:\n",
    "\n",
    "```bash\n",
    "export TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=\"123456:your-token\"\n",
    "export TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=\"@your_channel_username\"\n",
    "export GITHUB_REPOSITORY=\"your-username/your-public-repository\"\n",
    "jupyter lab\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "The bot must be an administrator in the channel. To delete its previous channel post, it needs the appropriate channel posting/deletion permissions.\n",
    "\n",
    "## How scheduled execution works\n",
    "\n",
    "GitHub Actions runs this notebook as a fresh process at each scheduled time. The workflow commits the updated `state.json` back to the repository so the next run knows which post to delete and which image was used last.\n"
   ]
  }
